        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Applications",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The synchronization onset is a **bifurcation** (Ch. 03): a supercritical transition at `K_c` from\nincoherence (`r=0`) to partial sync (`r>0` growing like `√(K−K_c)`) — the same square-root law as a\nsupercritical pitchfork/Hopf. This is a genuine *phase transition* in the `statistical-mechanics/`\nsense (the order parameter `r` is the magnetization analogue), making Kuramoto the bridge between\nnonlinear oscillation and collective phenomena. Applications: power-grid stability (loss of sync = a\nblackout), neural rhythms, clock distribution in distributed systems, and laser arrays."
    }
